# CodeBuddy can outlive its own failure, so the caller's task budget is not a
# usable guard. Measured 2026-09-21: the upstream gateway sent 1497 placeholder
# chunks (1.25 MB) carrying no model output, the CLI raised EmptyStreamError at
# 4m39s, and then sat at 0% CPU without ever exiting. The caller's default budget
# was 3600 s, so a run that was already dead held a workspace lock for an hour.
#
# A stall detector cannot tell that apart from healthy work here: the adapter runs
# with --output-format json, so a correct run also writes nothing to stdout until
# the very end. A wall-clock cap per mode is the only honest signal available.
#
# The numbers come from 64 recorded CodeBuddy runs, not from taste. Longest
# observed run per mode: implement 1689 s, advisory 552 s, review 329 s. Each cap
# keeps real headroom over that maximum; raise a cap only against new measured
# runs, never to rescue a single run that happened to hit it.
