# Adapters whose contractor shell is brokered by Fleet itself (grok through the
# grok_acp permission broker). The broker allowlist grok_acp.OFFICE_SHELL_SUBCOMMANDS
# permits only who, read, channels, presence and send - wait blocks the process
# until timeout and would deadlock a one-shot contractor whose parent waits on it,
# so wait/ack/delivery stay denied. A brokered contractor must never receive a
# preamble that names those commands (measured denial pattern 2026-09-20), and an
# mcp-profile brokered adapter stays on checkpoint-relay instead of getting a
# direct preamble it cannot act on.
